data:{"id":"407622e7-1382-4efe-82e7-64344b8125a0","response_type":"tool_result","content":"","done":false,"data":{"ambiguous_slugs":{"entity/linux-mint":["fed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581","fed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581"]},"duration_ms":3,"error":"","found_kbs":{"concept/open-source-operating-system":["fed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581"],"concept/unix-like-operating-system":["fed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581"],"entity/chrome-os":["fed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581"],"entity/freebsd":["fed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581"],"entity/linux":["fed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581"],"entity/linux-mint":["fed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581","fed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581"],"entity/ubuntu":["fed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581"],"summary/d4fdffd0-5c7d-4290-adbb-f5e1f7ae80b0":["fed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581"]},"output":"\u003cwiki_page\u003e\n\u003cmetadata\u003e\n\u003cknowledge_base_id\u003efed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581\u003c/knowledge_base_id\u003e\n\u003clink\u003e[[entity/ubuntu|Ubuntu]]\u003c/link\u003e\n\u003ctype\u003eentity\u003c/type\u003e\n\u003caliases\u003e\u003c/aliases\u003e\n\u003c/metadata\u003e\n\u003crelationships\u003e\n\u003clinks_to\u003e[[entity/linux]] (summary omitted, already seen), [[entity/linux-mint]] (summary omitted, already seen)\u003c/links_to\u003e\n\u003clinked_from\u003e[[summary/d4fdffd0-5c7d-4290-adbb-f5e1f7ae80b0]] (This document compares popular non-Windows operating systems, highlighting Linux distributions like Ubuntu and Mint, and noting the similarities between FreeBSD and Linux despite kernel differences.), [[concept/open-source-operating-system]] (summary omitted, already seen), [[entity/linux-mint]] (summary omitted, already seen), [[entity/linux]] (summary omitted, already seen)\u003c/linked_from\u003e\n\u003c/relationships\u003e\n\u003csources\u003e\n\u003csource knowledge_id=\"d4fdffd0-5c7d-4290-adbb-f5e1f7ae80b0\"/\u003e\n\u003c/sources\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003e\nUbuntu is a popular Linux distribution recommended for users seeking a non-Windows operating system for daily use on personal computers.\n\u003c/summary\u003e\n\u003ccontent\u003e\n# Ubuntu\n\nUbuntu is a popular [[entity/linux|Linux]] distribution. It is recommended for users seeking to install a non-Windows operating system on their personal computer for daily use. Along with [[entity/linux-mint|Linux Mint]], it stands out as one of the most popular choices within the Linux ecosystem.\n\u003c/content\u003e\n\u003c/wiki_page\u003e\n\n\u003cwiki_page\u003e\n\u003cmetadata\u003e\n\u003cknowledge_base_id\u003efed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581\u003c/knowledge_base_id\u003e\n\u003clink\u003e[[entity/linux-mint|Linux Mint]]\u003c/link\u003e\n\u003ctype\u003eentity\u003c/type\u003e\n\u003caliases\u003eMint\u003c/aliases\u003e\n\u003c/metadata\u003e\n\u003crelationships\u003e\n\u003clinks_to\u003e[[entity/linux]] (summary omitted, already seen), [[entity/ubuntu]] (summary omitted, already seen)\u003c/links_to\u003e\n\u003clinked_from\u003e[[summary/d4fdffd0-5c7d-4290-adbb-f5e1f7ae80b0]] (summary omitted, already seen), [[concept/open-source-operating-system]] (summary omitted, already seen), [[entity/ubuntu]] (summary omitted, already seen), [[entity/linux]] (summary omitted, already seen)\u003c/linked_from\u003e\n\u003c/relationships\u003e\n\u003csources\u003e\n\u003csource knowledge_id=\"d4fdffd0-5c7d-4290-adbb-f5e1f7ae80b0\"/\u003e\n\u003c/sources\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003e\nLinux Mint is a popular Linux distribution recommended for personal computers as a user-friendly, stable, and secure alternative to proprietary operating systems.\n\u003c/summary\u003e\n\u003ccontent\u003e\n# [[entity/linux|Linux]] Mint\n\nLinux Mint is a widely used Linux distribution cited as a top choice for personal computer installations. Along with [[entity/ubuntu|Ubuntu]], it is identified as one of the most popular distributions within the Linux ecosystem.\n\nThese systems provide a robust alternative to proprietary operating systems, offering stability, security, and a wide range of software support. Their popularity stems from user-friendly interfaces and extensive community support, making them ideal candidates for those transitioning away from Windows.\n\u003c/content\u003e\n\u003c/wiki_page\u003e\n\n\u003cwiki_page\u003e\n\u003cmetadata\u003e\n\u003cknowledge_base_id\u003efed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581\u003c/knowledge_base_id\u003e\n\u003clink\u003e[[entity/freebsd|FreeBSD]]\u003c/link\u003e\n\u003ctype\u003eentity\u003c/type\u003e\n\u003caliases\u003e\u003c/aliases\u003e\n\u003c/metadata\u003e\n\u003crelationships\u003e\n\u003clinks_to\u003e[[entity/linux]] (summary omitted, already seen)\u003c/links_to\u003e\n\u003clinked_from\u003e[[concept/unix-like-operating-system]] (summary omitted, already seen), [[concept/open-source-operating-system]] (summary omitted, already seen), [[entity/linux]] (summary omitted, already seen)\u003c/linked_from\u003e\n\u003c/relationships\u003e\n\u003csources\u003e\n\u003csource knowledge_id=\"d4fdffd0-5c7d-4290-adbb-f5e1f7ae80b0\"/\u003e\n\u003c/sources\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003e\nFreeBSD is an open-source operating system that uses a different kernel than Linux but shares much of the same software ecosystem, offering a similar desktop experience.\n\u003c/summary\u003e\n\u003ccontent\u003e\n# FreeBSD\n\nFreeBSD is an open-source operating system. Although it utilizes a different kernel compared to [[entity/linux|Linux]], the user experience on a desktop PC is remarkably similar. This similarity arises because FreeBSD shares much of the same software ecosystem found in typical Linux distributions. Users familiar with Linux will find the transition to FreeBSD relatively smooth, as the applications and tools they rely on are largely compatible or have direct equivalents.\n\u003c/content\u003e\n\u003c/wiki_page\u003e\n\n\u003cwiki_page\u003e\n\u003cmetadata\u003e\n\u003cknowledge_base_id\u003efed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581\u003c/knowledge_base_id\u003e\n\u003clink\u003e[[entity/chrome-os|Chrome OS]]\u003c/link\u003e\n\u003ctype\u003eentity\u003c/type\u003e\n\u003caliases\u003e铬操作系统\u003c/aliases\u003e\n\u003c/metadata\u003e\n\u003crelationships\u003e\n\u003clinks_to\u003e(none)\u003c/links_to\u003e\n\u003clinked_from\u003e[[concept/open-source-operating-system]] (summary omitted, already seen), [[entity/linux]] (summary omitted, already seen)\u003c/linked_from\u003e\n\u003c/relationships\u003e\n\u003csources\u003e\n\u003csource knowledge_id=\"d4fdffd0-5c7d-4290-adbb-f5e1f7ae80b0\"/\u003e\n\u003c/sources\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003e\nChrome OS is an operating system mentioned as an alternative to Windows for personal computers, listed alongside Linux and FreeBSD in discussions of non-Windows computing platforms.\n\u003c/summary\u003e\n\u003ccontent\u003e\n# Chrome OS\n\nChrome OS (referred to as \"铬操作系统\" in some sources) is an operating system mentioned in the context of alternative PC operating systems. It is listed alongside other major non-Windows operating systems, indicating its relevance in the broader discussion of alternative computing platforms.\n\u003c/content\u003e\n\u003c/wiki_page\u003e","success":true,"tool_call_id":"call_5d01649566ff49429bd58194","tool_name":"wiki_read_page"}}

